  "observations": [
    {
      "dimension": "Visible clearing",
      "observation": "Each before-stop image visibly contains photographed hand joints. The after-stop and settled images show only the ordinary camera-off empty state, with no retained mint hand overlay over its icon or title. Correct camera-off and cleared-session text are visible."
    },
    {
      "dimension": "Idle and resize continuity",
      "observation": "Actual trace frames corroborate that camera-off remains blank after settling and after changing the viewport from 1280 by 800 to 950 by 720. No automatic camera reactivation is observed before explicit enable."
    },
    {
      "dimension": "Fresh restart and second clearing",
      "observation": "Actual trace frames show a new photographed camera image and fresh visible joints after explicit reactivation, followed by a second stop returning to the blank camera-off empty state."
    },
    {
      "dimension": "Canvas alpha support",
      "observation": "Scalar evidence supplements direct visual inspection: camera visible pixels are positive before stop, zero after stop, zero after settling and resize, positive after explicit reactivation, then zero after the second stop at both DPR values. The pointer canvas is already empty in these focused cases and stays empty."
    },
    {
      "dimension": "Resources and process lifecycle",
      "observation": "Both scalar receipts report zero owned tracks and workers in the stopped settled state. The terminal supplemental receipt reports 2 expected passes, no unexpected or skipped cases, unchanged source/fixture/build, browser and server cleanup passing, released port and archived owned mutable runtime."
    },
    {
      "dimension": "Capture interpretation",
      "observation": "Full-page PNGs show the fixed shell displaced through the page during capture. Proper viewport trace frames corroborate the blank camera stage, restart and second stop. This review does not classify that screenshot presentation as a new application defect or accept the overall shell layout from those full-page images."
    }
  ],
